divergence_reason = sanctioned: Go backend codegen bug for a function value boxed through `Ok`/`Just` — the same silently-wrong-result class documented in l0114_maybe_and_map_fn_payload / l0114_result_and_map_fn_payload (the `interface{}`-boxed function is never actually invoked by the Go `andMap` kernel). Here the payload flows through an unannotated same-module double forwarder before reaching `Result.andMap`: correct output is `42` (`inc 41`), but the compiled Go binary (verified against /usr/local/bin/sky v0.16.29) prints `41` — the payload passed through unapplied. Rust's `Box<dyn Fn>` kernel call computes the semantically correct value. Divergence from Sky, rationale: Go backend bug (not a Sky-Rust behavior choice).
